# No context in structs

Do not put `context.Context` on structs (including job/request DTOs queued for later). Pass `ctx` as the first parameter and cancel via the pal run context or request scope.

**Linter:** [containedctx](https://github.com/sivchari/containedctx) — enabled in `.golangci.yaml` via `linters.default: all` (not in `disable`).

```go
// BAD — ctx stored for async work
type deliveryJob struct {
	ctx context.Context
	env core.Envelope
}

// GOOD — queue payload only; workers receive ctx from Run(ctx)
func (e *Engine) workerLoop(ctx context.Context, w *targetWorker) {
	for env := range w.queue {
		e.deliver(ctx, w, env)
	}
}
```

Rare exceptions (HTTP `Request`, generated code) may use `//nolint:containedctx` with a one-line reason.
